+## Genetic Algorithm NSGA-II Filters
+
+NSGA-II carries filter outcomes separately from scalar energy. Rejected proposals
+skip scoring and have no objective vector; they rank after every eligible proposal,
+even if their penalty is finite or inherited metadata contains older scores. They
+may fill unused working-population slots so mutation can recover feasibility, but
+are excluded from accepted results. Fewer than `num_results` (including zero) can
+be returned if too few pass. Missing, nonfinite or flagged fallback objectives on
+eligible proposals remain errors.
